  "term": "social code",
  "definition": "In this context, the Social Code refers to German social legislation, specifically Social Code Book V. It includes a provision (§64b) that allows cross-sector, patient-centered psychiatric care models using a shared per-patient budget across inpatient and outpatient treatment.",
